// Cross-topic consolidation for Unit 2 topics 3.2.7, 3.2.8 and 3.2.9 (Phase 4 Batch 3, cluster author ACL3).
// Theme: mass transport and what happens when it fails or is exploited. Blood carries oxygen to cardiac muscle through the
// coronary arteries (3.2.6.2, Unit 1 3.1.5.3) until atheroma and thrombosis interrupt it (3.2.7); xylem and phloem move
// water and sucrose by water potential and pressure gradients (3.2.8, Unit 1 3.1.4.2 and 3.1.4.3); aphids tap the
// pressurised phloem and carry viruses between immobile plants (3.2.9, with 3.2.1.1 and 3.2.4.1).
// Scope follows PHASE4_BATCH3_MANIFEST.md: cohesion–tension, the Casparian strip, sieve tube structure, H⁺ co-transport in
// loading, persistent and non-persistent transmission, named viruses and the systemic movement of viruses in the phloem
// are labelled supporting. Co-transport is a Unit 2 statement (3.2.2.3.s2, with sodium ions in the ileum), not Unit 1.
// Unit 1 nodes carry "Unit 1 ·" in their reference. Nothing here is medical advice or a personal risk tool.
// Question ids q-cl27-… and card ids f-cl27-… are unique site-wide. Real data are cited; everything else is labelled
